abstract: >-
  A benchmarking framework for ML inference across heterogeneous hardware. One
  configuration file and one command execute an experiment matrix across any mix of
  machines, over SSH or locally, and every measurement returns as a single
  self-describing JSON record carrying the hardware, OS, kernel, compiler, backend
  version and build commit, model, quantization, the metrics, and the physical state of
  the machine while they were taken: per-rail power, temperature, clocks, throttle flags
  and memory pressure. It measures time to first token, prefill and decode throughput,
  request latency percentiles, peak resident memory, and derives decode bandwidth and
  roofline utilization. Run identifiers are deterministic over the specification, so an
  interrupted campaign resumes and a corrected point re-executes exactly, and failures
  are records with their raw output preserved rather than exceptions. The analysis layer
  turns a directory of records into publication-quality tables and figures.
